    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-6",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-6",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Burn injury history and reported symptoms"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Electrical arc/flash at work 3 days ago while isolating a switchboard; tool slipped. Patient reports intense heat to face and anterior neck, immediate redness and tightness over cheeks, nose, forehead and anterior neck, and small blisters on both upper cheeks on day 1 that ruptured spontaneously. Now dry, tight skin with mild pain, approximately 3/10, described as more annoying than anything."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-7",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-7",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Associated injury events"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Patient reports no direct contact with live wires, loss of consciousness, fall, head strike, or clothing ignition."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-8",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-8",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Facial and neck skin examination"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Forehead, nasal bridge, both malar areas, anterior neck and upper chest involved. Clear T-shirt line and safety-glasses border pattern; appearance consistent with flash burn rather than prolonged contact or pure sunburn. Forehead, nose and neck erythematous, warm and mildly tender, with intact sensation. Both upper cheeks have 2–3 cm areas of healing superficial partial-thickness burns where blisters have ruptured; areas are pink and moist, with no slough or pus. Skin is soft with no circumferential neck burn or tight eschar. No charring; minimal singeing of eyebrows and sideburns. No clinical cellulitis at present. Burn depth appears mainly superficial to superficial partial thickness."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-9",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-9",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Estimated burn surface area"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Estimated TBSA approximately 5–6%; supervisor addendum estimates approximately 5%."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-10",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-10",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Eye symptoms"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "After a brief bright flash, patient saw spots for a few minutes, which settled. Mild grittiness in both eyes occurred the first night only and has resolved. Currently denies eye pain, photophobia, blurred vision, foreign-body sensation, or reduced vision."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-11",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-11",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Eye examination"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "No periorbital oedema; lids open fully and no burns at lid margins. Conjunctiva mildly injected, without chemosis. PERRLA, EOMI; visual acuity grossly normal and patient able to read a poster. No photophobia."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-12",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-12",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Airway and respiratory symptoms"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Denies hoarseness, dysphagia, shortness of breath at the time of injury or since, cough, or soot in the mouth."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-13",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-13",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "ENT and airway examination"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Oropharynx clear, with no soot or marked posterior pharyngeal erythema. Voice normal, no stridor; neck supple and trachea midline. No evidence of airway involvement documented."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-14",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-14",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Systemic symptoms"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Denies fever, chills, nausea, or vomiting; reports feeling otherwise well."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-15",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-15",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "General examination"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Alert and well appearing, speaking in full sentences, no acute distress."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-16",
      "resource": {
        "resourceType": "Observation",
        "id": "observation-16",
        "status": "final",
        "code": {
          "text": "Cardiovascular, respiratory and neurological examination"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Heart sounds dual with no added sounds. Chest clear bilaterally. Neurological examination grossly non-focal; gait normal."
      }
    },
    {
      "fullUrl": "https://example.org/fhir/Observation/observation-17",
      "resource": {
